 13.9292 8.56974 13.9619 8.9707C13.9987 9.42092 13.998 9.97799 13.998 10.667V12.665ZM18.165 9.33301C18.165 10.022 18.1657 10.5791 18.1289 11.0293C18.0961 11.4302 18.0311 11.7914 17.8867 12.1279L17.8203 12.2705C17.5549 12.7914 17.1509 13.2272 16.6553 13.5313L16.4365 13.6533C16.0599 13.8452 15.6541 13.9245 15.1963 13.9619C14.8593 13.9895 14.4624 13.9935 13.9951 13.9951C13.9935 14.4624 13.9895 14.8593 13.9619 15.1963C13.9292 15.597 13.864 15.9576 13.7197 16.2939L13.6533 16.4365C13.3878 16.9576 12.9841 17.3941 12.4883 17.6982L12.2705 17.8203C11.8937 18.0123 11.4873 18.0915 11.0293 18.1289C10.5791 18.1657 10.022 18.165 9.33301 18.165H6.5C5.81091 18.165 5.25395 18.1657 4.80371 18.1289C4.40306 18.0962 4.04235 18.031 3.70606 17.8867L3.56348 17.8203C3.04244 17.5548 2.60585 17.151 2.30176 16.6553L2.17969 16.4365C1.98788 16.0599 1.90851 15.6541 1.87109 15.1963C1.83431 14.746 1.83496 14.1891 1.83496 13.5V10.667C1.83496 9.978 1.83432 9.42091 1.87109 8.9707C1.90851 8.5127 1.98772 8.10625 2.17969 7.72949L2.30176 7.51172C2.60586 7.0159 3.04236 6.6122 3.56348 6.34668L3.70606 6.28027C4.04237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg></button></span></div></div></div></div>
<p data-start="4692" data-end="4836">This is a shift from <strong data-start="4713" data-end="4744">“language generates itself”</strong> to <strong data-start="4748" data-end="4836">“language generates constrained world-models that generate plausible continuations.”</strong></p>
<p data-start="4838" data-end="4899">Much stronger. Much truer to both cognition and LLM behavior.</p>
<hr data-start="4901" data-end="4904">
<h1 data-start="4906" data-end="4967"><strong data-start="4908" data-end="4967">8. If you wanted to compress it into a thesis paragraph</strong></h1>
<blockquote data-start="4969" data-end="5564">
<p data-start="4971" data-end="5564"><em data-start="4971" data-end="5564">Language is a sparse predictive interface to shared perceptual models, not a combinatorial generator of meaning. Understanding does not explore all interpretations, it eliminates most based on a compressed world prior. Semantics are organized so that conceptual proximity mirrors temporal and causal adjacency, allowing reasoning to unfold as a local traversal through predictive proxy models rather than an exhaustive search. In this view, next-token prediction succeeds not because language is self-generating, but because language semi-encodes the simulator that speakers jointly inhabit.</em></p>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start="5566" data-end="5569">
<p data-start="5571" data-end="5596">If you want, next we can:</p>
<ol data-start="5598" data-end="5912">
<li data-start="5598" data-end="5690">
<p data-start="5601" data-end="5690">formalize this mathematically (information geometry, predictive coding, sparse inference)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5691" data-end="5793">
<p data-start="5694" data-end="5793">map it to transformer mechanisms (attention as trajectory selection, logits as constrained futures)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5794" data-end="5837">
<p data-start="5797" data-end="5837">compare it to child language acquisition</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5838" data-end="5871">
<p data-start="5841" data-end="5871">derive falsifiable predictions</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5872" data-end="5912">
<p data-start="5875" data-end="5912">or write it as a polished short essay</p>
</li>
