<p data-start="5565" data-end="5641">where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_j</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7167em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02691em;">w</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0269em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> are attention weights and <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo>⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">ϕ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">⋅</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> are value encodings.</p>
<h3 data-start="5643" data-end="5691">logits, softmax, and mixture-of-experts view</h3>
<p data-start="5692" data-end="5965">The final linear+softmax head produces logits <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z = W_o h_T</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.04398em;">z</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8444em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">W</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.1389em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">o</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">h</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_T</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8444em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">h</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is the final representation. Because <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_T</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8444em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">h</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">T</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is an attention-weighted aggregate of past snippets, logits can be seen as a mixture of conditional distributions contributed by the retrieved snippets:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≈</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mtext> </mtext><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat p(x_{t+1}\mid x_{\le t}) \approx \sum_j \alpha_{j}\, p_j(x_{t+1}),</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord accent"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6944em;"><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span></span><span style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="accent-body" style="left: -0.1667em;"><span class="mord">^</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1944em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2952em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mrel mtight">≤</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2452em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.4638em; vertical-align: -1.4138em;"></span><span class="mop op-limits"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.05em;"><span style="top: -1.8723em; margin-left: 0em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3.05em;"></span><span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op">∑</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 1.4138em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0037em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="6044" data-end="6147">a <strong data-start="6046" data-end="6078">sparse mixture-of-predictors</strong> where <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_j</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7167em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0037em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is sparse if attention focuses on a few contexts.</p>
<h3 data-start="6149" data-end="6205">in-context learning as gradient-free Bayesian update</h3>
<p data-start="6206" data-end="6463">Few-shot examples appear in the context and are stored as <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_j,v_j</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9805em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0315em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">v</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. Attention reallocates weights so that these examples have strong influence when a matching query occurs. Mechanistically this is a <em data-start="6408" data-end="6462">fast, transient, attention-mediated posterior update</em>:</p>
<ul data-start="6464" data-end="6714">
<li data-start="6464" data-end="6504">
<p data-start="6466" data-end="6504">No weight updates are needed (no SGD).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6505" data-end="6714">
<p data-start="6507" data-end="6714">The attention distribution implements a local reweighting that acts like conditioning on examples.<br>
Thus in-context generalization is approximate Bayesian conditioning performed by attention over the KV bank.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="6716" data-end="6761">recursive templates &amp; algorithm emulation</h3>
<p data-start="6762" data-end="6850">Transformers can implement iterative/recursive computation through architectural motifs:</p>
<ul data-start="6851" data-end="7487">
<li data-start="6851" data-end="6952">
<p data-start="6853" data-end="6952">Stacked layers + residual connections produce repeated nonlinear transforms (iterative refinement).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6953" data-end="7100">
<p data-start="6955" data-end="7100">Multi-head attention provides parallelized addressing and routing (different heads can play role: program counter, stack pointer, content store).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7101" data-end="7487">
<p data-start="7103" data-end="7487">Learned addressing patterns (e.g., attention focusing on previous special tokens) can emulate pushdown behavior: use read/write-like patterns across positions to simulate stack pushes/pops across layers/time.<br>
In practice this yields emergent behaviors resembling recursion or short programs executed in context (the model “routes” through the KV graph following attention affinities).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="7489" data-end="7554">top-k / top-p sampling = explicit sparse hypothesis selection</h3>
<p data-start="7555" data-end="7895">Sampling strategies such as top-k/top-p select a small subset of tokens from the predictive distribution. Functionally this enforces <em data-start="7688" data-end="7712">sparse decision making</em>: among the many possible continuations implied by the posterior over <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">h</span></span></span></span>, the model picks a small set of candidate continuations to realize — exactly the sparse traversal behavior.</p>
<h1 data-start="7897" data-end="7920">Short summary mapping</h1>
<ul data-start="7922" data-end="8539">
<li data-start="7922" data-end="8039">
<p data-start="7924" data-end="8039">Posterior over latent templates <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(h\mid x_{\le t})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">h</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2952em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mrel mtight">≤</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2452em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>  ←→  attention weights <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7167em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0037em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">ij</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> over stored contexts.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8040" data-end="8178">
<p data-start="8042" data-end="8178">Predictive marginalization <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int p(x_{t+1}\mid s) p(s\mid x_{\le t}) ds</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1111em; vertical-align: -0.3061em;"></span><span class="mop op-symbol small-op" style="margin-right: 0.19445em; position: relative; top: -0.0006em;">∫</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span><span class="mbin mtight">+</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">s</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">s</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2952em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mrel mtight">≤</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2452em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">s</span></span></span></span>  ←→  logits computed from attention-aggregated value vectors.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8179" data-end="8320">
<p data-start="8181" data-end="8320">Holographic, distributed evidence  ←→  many weak embedding cues <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_j</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7167em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">e</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> whose combined dot-products/nested attention sum to strong support.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8321" data-end="8452">
<p data-start="8323" data-end="8452">Sparse interpretation / few hypotheses  ←→  attention focusing (and top-k/top-p sampling) producing low-entropy predictive mixes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8453" data-end="8539">
<p data-start="8455" data-end="8539">In-context learning  ←→  KV reweighting as a transient, associative Bayesian update.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h1 data-start="8541" data-end="8609">3. Short list of falsifiable predictions / experiments (practical)</h1>
<ol data-start="8611" data-end="10252">
<li data-start="8611" data-end="9001">
<p data-start="8614" data-end="9001"><strong data-start="8614" data-end="8651">Synthetic-corpus algorithm probe.</strong> Construct a corpus where a simple recursive algorithm (e.g., balanced-parentheses checker or stack-like rewrite rule) is embedded <em data-start="8782" data-end="8795">only weakly</em> across many contexts (distributed cues). Train next-token model: if the proxy/holographic thesis holds, the model should recover the algorithm at some scale; measure how cue density affects recoverability.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9003" data-end="9312">
<p data-start="9006" data-end="9312"><strong data-start="9006" data-end="9046">Attention-posterior alignment probe.</strong> Train a probe that maps attention distributions <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7167em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0037em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">ij</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> to explicit posterior beliefs over a small hypothesis set <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal H</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.00965em;">H</span></span></span></span> (constructed for the task). If attention truly approximates posterior weights, the probe should predict the true posterior well.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9314" data-end="9649">
<p data-start="9317" data-end="9649"><strong data-start="9317" data-end="9345">Ablate inductive biases.</strong> Remove/alter positional encodings or change attention softmax temperature/normalization and measure sample complexity needed to recover the same templates. If templates are holographically encoded in corpus, the right inductive biases will lower required sample complexity but not be strictly necessary.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9651" data-end="9897">
<p data-start="9654" data-end="9897"><strong data-start="9654" data-end="9680">KV bank sparsity test.</strong> Force a transformer to use a very long context but penalize attention entropy (encourage sparse α). Compare performance vs. unconstrained model: improved or unchanged performance supports sparse traversal hypothesis.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9899" data-end="10252">
<p data-start="9902" data-end="10252"><strong data-start="9902" data-end="9937">Cross-community variation test.</strong> Build corpora that encode different procedural templates (e.g., one culture’s recipes vs. another’s). Train identical models and test for the specific algorithmic behaviors predicted by each corpus — if language folds algorithms into its statistics, models should internalize culture-specific procedural templates.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h1 data-start="10254" data-end="10287">4. Minimal concluding statement</h1>
<p data-start="10288" data-end="10967">Formally: language corpora instantiate evidentiary distributions over latent predictive templates <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">h</span></span></span></span>; next-token learners implement approximate posterior inference over those templates via attention and KV retrieval, producing <em data-start="10518" data-end="10557">sparse, context-conditioned traversal</em> of meaning rather than exhaustive search. Mechanistically, attention + residual stacks + softmax sampling are exactly the primitives required to (1) integrate distributed weak cues, (2) select a small set of active hypotheses, and (3) execute their continuations as next-token predictions — which yields the appearance of recursion, reasoning, and algorithmic competence without any explicit external program.</p>
<hr data-start="10969" data-end="10972">
<p data-start="10974" data-end="10997">If you want, I can now:</p>
<ul data-start="10998" data-end="11390" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">
<li data-start="10998" data-end="11161">
<p data-start="11000" data-end="11161">expand any of the equations into a longer derivation (e.g., show the free-energy minimizer for a simple Markov latent state and how attention approximates it),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="11162" data-end="11267">
<p data-start="11164" data-end="11267">write a short experimental script outline (pseudo-code) for the synthetic-corpus experiment above, or</p>
</li>
<li data-start="11268" data-end="11390" data-is-last-node="">
<p data-start="11270" data-end="11390" data-is-last-node="">produce a compact paper-style paragraph you can paste into a Substack or working paper. Which would be most useful next?</p>
</li>
</ul></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5.7889