If we treat positions (j) as independent evidence fragments, the product of likelihoods corresponds to summing logs. Attention’s normalized exponential over many (j) therefore gives weights proportional to local likelihood contributions; and the weighted sum of the (v_j) (which we assume encodes future predictive distributions) approximates mixture marginalization:
[
