7728 13.3878 7.20854 13.6533 7.72949L13.7197 7.87207C13.8642 8.20859 13.9292 8.56974 13.9619 8.9707C13.9987 9.42092 13.998 9.97799 13.998 10.667V12.665ZM18.165 9.33301C18.165 10.022 18.1657 10.5791 18.1289 11.0293C18.0961 11.4302 18.0311 11.7914 17.8867 12.1279L17.8203 12.2705C17.5549 12.7914 17.1509 13.2272 16.6553 13.5313L16.4365 13.6533C16.0599 13.8452 15.6541 13.9245 15.1963 13.9619C14.8593 13.9895 14.4624 13.9935 13.9951 13.9951C13.9935 14.4624 13.9895 14.8593 13.9619 15.1963C13.9292 15.597 13.864 15.9576 13.7197 16.2939L13.6533 16.4365C13.3878 16.9576 12.9841 17.3941 12.4883 17.6982L12.2705 17.8203C11.8937 18.0123 11.4873 18.0915 11.0293 18.1289C10.5791 18.1657 10.022 18.165 9.33301 18.165H6.5C5.81091 18.165 5.25395 18.1657 4.80371 18.1289C4.40306 18.0962 4.04235 18.031 3.70606 17.8867L3.56348 17.8203C3.04244 17.5548 2.60585 17.151 2.30176 16.6553L2.17969 16.4365C1.98788 16.0599 1.90851 15.6541 1.87109 15.1963C1.83431 14.746 1.83496 14.1891 1.83496 13.5V10.667C1.83496 9.978 1.83432 9.42091 1.87109 8.9707C1.90851 8.5127 1.98772 8.10625 2.17969 7.72949L2.30176 7.51172C2.60586 7.0159 3.04236 6.6122 3.56348 6.34668L3.70606 6.28027C4.04237 6.136 4.40303 6.07083 4.80371 6.03809C5.14051 6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg></button></span></div></div></div></div>
<p data-start="2781" data-end="2906">Both categories assume language is <em data-start="2816" data-end="2838">about something else</em>—either an innate formal system or a learned communication protocol.</p>
<p data-start="2908" data-end="2940">The new hypothesis inverts this:</p>
<blockquote data-start="2942" data-end="3099">
<p data-start="2944" data-end="3099"><strong data-start="2944" data-end="3099">Language is not the description of cognition—language is one of the primary spaces where cognition is serialized, stored, refined, and re-instantiated.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="3101" data-end="3114">In this view:</p>
<ul data-start="3116" data-end="3544">
<li data-start="3116" data-end="3211">
<p data-start="3118" data-end="3211">Grammars are emergent <em data-start="3140" data-end="3181">constraints on predictive compatibility</em>, not pre-defined rule engines</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3212" data-end="3294">
<p data-start="3214" data-end="3294">Meaning is <em data-start="3225" data-end="3271">activation of shared predictive world-models</em>, not dictionary lookup</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3295" data-end="3394">
<p data-start="3297" data-end="3394">Understanding is <em data-start="3314" data-end="3371">narrowing a posterior over plausible world trajectories</em>, not selecting symbols</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3395" data-end="3492">
<p data-start="3397" data-end="3492">Reasoning is <em data-start="3410" data-end="3465">path traversal through a semantic predictive manifold</em>, not search in logic space</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3493" data-end="3544">
<p data-start="3495" data-end="3544">Concepts are <em data-start="3508" data-end="3532">compressed simulations</em>, not labels</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3546" data-end="3694">This reconception aligns language with <strong data-start="3585" data-end="3646">prediction, compression, model selection, and computation</strong>, rather than reference and symbol manipulation.</p>
<hr data-start="3696" data-end="3699">
<h2 data-start="3701" data-end="3755"><strong data-start="3704" data-end="3755">3. Intellectual lineage and adjacent frameworks</strong></h2>
<p data-start="3757" data-end="3856">This hypothesis does not arise in a vacuum. It sits at the convergence of several lines of thought:</p>
<h3 data-start="3858" data-end="3911"><strong data-start="3862" data-end="3911">Predictive processing (Friston, Clark, Hohwy)</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="3912" data-end="4097">
<li data-start="3912" data-end="3983">
<p data-start="3914" data-end="3983">The brain minimizes prediction error rather than manipulating symbols</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3984" data-end="4050">
<p data-start="3986" data-end="4050">Perception and cognition are forms of generative model inversion</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4051" data-end="4097">
<p data-start="4053" data-end="4097">Language likely taps into the same machinery</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="4099" data-end="4161"><strong data-start="4103" data-end="4161">Bayesian program learning (Lake, Tenenbaum, Griffiths)</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="4162" data-end="4287">
<li data-start="4162" data-end="4213">
<p data-start="4164" data-end="4213">Humans infer latent programs from sparse evidence</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4214" data-end="4287">
<p data-start="4216" data-end="4287">Concepts behave like composable generative functions, not feature lists</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="4289" data-end="4356"><strong data-start="4293" data-end="4356">Distributional semantics (Harris → word2vec → transformers)</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="4357" data-end="4449">
<li data-start="4357" data-end="4379">
<p data-start="4359" data-end="4379">“Meaning is context”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4380" data-end="4449">
<p data-start="4382" data-end="4449">But the deeper implication is: <em data-start="4413" data-end="4449">context forms a navigable geometry</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="4451" data-end="4514"><strong data-start="4455" data-end="4514">Algorithmic information theory (Solomonoff, Kolmogorov)</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="4515" data-end="4646">
<li data-start="4515" data-end="4582">
<p data-start="4517" data-end="4582">Shortest program consistent with the data is the best explanation</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4583" data-end="4646">
<p data-start="4585" data-end="4646">Language compresses cultural programs into transmittable form</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="4648" data-end="4725"><strong data-start="4652" data-end="4725">Iterated learning &amp; cultural evolution (Kirby, Tamariz, Christiansen)</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="4726" data-end="4888">
<li data-start="4726" data-end="4819">
<p data-start="4728" data-end="4819">Languages evolve to maximize <em data-start="4757" data-end="4788">learnability and expressivity</em> under transmission bottlenecks</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4820" data-end="4888">
<p data-start="4822" data-end="4888">Culture crystallizes reusable inferences into linguistic structure</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="4890" data-end="4924"><strong data-start="4894" data-end="4924">Connectionism rediscovered</strong></h3>
<p data-start="4925" data-end="5158">Once dismissed for failing to handle systematicity, connectionist architectures (transformers) now <strong data-start="5024" data-end="5093">exhibit systematic generalization without explicit symbolic rules</strong>, by rediscovering algorithms latent in distributional structure.</p>
<hr data-start="5160" data-end="5163">
<h2 data-start="5165" data-end="5207"><strong data-start="5168" data-end="5207">4. Core theoretical claim (refined)</strong></h2>
<p data-start="5209" data-end="5269">We assemble the elements into a precise, non-mystical claim:</p>
<h3 data-start="5271" data-end="5350"><strong data-start="5275" data-end="5350">(A) Language is a cultural compression of reusable inference procedures</strong></h3>
<p data-start="5351" data-end="5478">Not merely <em data-start="5362" data-end="5373">knowledge</em>, but <em data-start="5379" data-end="5438">ways of predicting, explaining, inferring, and simulating</em> are encoded in linguistic regularities.</p>
<h3 data-start="5480" data-end="5535"><strong data-start="5484" data-end="5535">(B) These procedures are stored holographically</strong></h3>
<p data-start="5536" data-end="5656">No single phrase contains the full rule, but <strong data-start="5581" data-end="5655">many weak, distributed cues jointly identify the same latent algorithm</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start="5658" data-end="5693"><strong data-start="5662" data-end="5693">(C) Understanding is sparse</strong></h3>
<p data-start="5694" data-end="5804">Humans and models do <strong data-start="5715" data-end="5743">not explore all meanings</strong>, but sharply prune interpretations using context as a prior.</p>
<h3 data-start="5806" data-end="5842"><strong data-start="5810" data-end="5842">(D) Semantics is geometrized</strong></h3>
<p data-start="5843" data-end="5942">Conceptual adjacency in meaning corresponds to <strong data-start="5890" data-end="5941">navigable proximity in linguistic context space</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start="5944" data-end="6009"><strong data-start="5948" data-end="6009">(E) Next-token training performs implicit model selection</strong></h3>
<p data-start="6010" data-end="6104">Transformers approximate a posterior over latent predictive templates and then sample from it.</p>
<p data-start="6106" data-end="6272">This does <em data-start="6116" data-end="6121">not</em> claim the model has agency, grounding, or human-like implementation—only that the <em data-start="6204" data-end="6239">functional structure of inference</em> can be absorbed from text alone.</p>
<hr data-start="6274" data-end="6277">
<h2 data-start="6279" data-end="6323"><strong data-start="6282" data-end="6323">5. Mechanistic bridge to transformers</strong></h2>
<p data-start="6325" data-end="6377">Transformers supply exactly the operations required:</p>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="6379" data-end="6837" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="6379" data-end="6431"><tr data-start="6379" data-end="6431"><th data-start="6379" data-end="6403" data-col-size="sm">Transformer Mechanism</th><th data-start="6403" data-end="6431" data-col-size="md">Cognitive Interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="6442" data-end="6837"><tr data-start="6442" data-end="6498"><td data-start="6442" data-end="6461" data-col-size="sm">Token embeddings</td><td data-start="6461" data-end="6498" data-col-size="md">compressed contextual affordances</td></tr><tr data-start="6499" data-end="6568"><td data-start="6499" data-end="6519" data-col-size="sm">Attention weights</td><td data-start="6519" data-end="6568" data-col-size="md">soft posterior over relevant evidentiary cues</td></tr><tr data-start="6569" data-end="6618"><td data-start="6569" data-end="6585" data-col-size="sm">Value vectors</td><td data-start="6585" data-end="6618" data-col-size="md">reusable predictive fragments</td></tr><tr data-start="6619" data-end="6672"><td data-start="6619" data-end="6640" data-col-size="sm">Multi-head routing</td><td data-start="6640" data-end="6672" data-col-size="md">parallel hypothesis channels</td></tr><tr data-start="6673" data-end="6727"><td data-start="6673" data-end="6690" data-col-size="sm">Layer stacking</td><td data-start="6690" data-end="6727" data-col-size="md">iterative refinement of inference</td></tr><tr data-start="6728" data-end="6782"><td data-start="6728" data-end="6737" data-col-size="sm">Logits</td><td data-start="6737" data-end="6782" data-col-size="md">predictive futures constrained by context</td></tr><tr data-start="6783" data-end="6837"><td data-start="6783" data-end="6806" data-col-size="sm">Top-k/top-p sampling</td><td data-start="6806" data-end="6837" data-col-size="md">sparse hypothesis selection</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5.78896 16.835 6.5 16.835H9.33301C10.0439 16.835 10.5374 16.8341 10.9209 16.8027C11.2965 16.772 11.508 16.7152 11.666 16.6348L11.793 16.5645C12.0804 16.3881 12.3148 16.1351 12.4688 15.833L12.5244 15.7031C12.5759 15.5594 12.6137 15.3698 12.6367 15.0879C12.6681 14.7044 12.668 14.211 12.668 13.5V10.667ZM13.998 12.665C14.4528 12.6634 14.8011 12.6602 15.0879 12.6367C15.4635 12.606 15.675 12.5492 15.833 12.4688L15.959 12.3975C16.2466 12.2211 16.4808 11.9682 16.6348 11.666L16.6914 11.5361C16.7428 11.3924 16.7797 11.2026 16.8027 10.9209C16.8341 10.5374 16.835 10.0439 16.835 9.33301V6.5C16.835 5.78896 16.8341 5.29563 16.8027 4.91211C16.7797 4.63025 16.