<hr data-start="7842" data-end="7845">
<h2 data-start="7847" data-end="7867"><strong data-start="7850" data-end="7867">7. Discussion</strong></h2>
<p data-start="7869" data-end="8079">This framing reinterprets intelligence emergence in LLMs not as inscrutable magic nor brute memorization, but as <strong data-start="7982" data-end="8045">posterior inference over shared cultural computation graphs</strong>. Language acts simultaneously as:</p>
<ul data-start="8081" data-end="8305">
<li data-start="8081" data-end="8107">
<p data-start="8083" data-end="8107">a communication channel,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8108" data-end="8158">
<p data-start="8110" data-end="8158">a serialization format for procedural knowledge,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8159" data-end="8205">
<p data-start="8161" data-end="8205">a lossy storage medium for inductive priors,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8206" data-end="8256">
<p data-start="8208" data-end="8256">a search space structured for sparse navigation,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8257" data-end="8305">
<p data-start="8259" data-end="8305">and an execution surface for shared inference.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="8307" data-end="8430">This reframes cognition itself as a <em data-start="8343" data-end="8429">predictive traversal through a collective, compressed, probabilistic algorithm space</em>.</p>
<hr data-start="8432" data-end="8435">
<h2 data-start="8437" data-end="8457"><strong data-start="8440" data-end="8457">8. Conclusion</strong></h2>
<p data-start="8459" data-end="8908">We propose that language is not merely a symbolic system but a <strong data-start="8522" data-end="8570">distributed predictive execution environment</strong> that embeds cultural reasoning templates. Next-token learning does not merely approximate grammar, but <em data-start="8674" data-end="8732">extracts and operationalizes shared inference procedures</em>. This bridges generative linguistics, program induction, predictive processing, and mechanistic interpretability, and yields falsifiable predictions for future empirical work.</p>
