he body of the paper (for intellectual priority and framing) and in the reference list.</p>
<p data-start="157" data-end="220">Since Barenholtz’s work relevant to this topic is primarily in:</p>
<ul data-start="222" data-end="398">
<li data-start="222" data-end="296">
<p data-start="224" data-end="296">talks and public lectures (e.g., cognitive/linguistic structure of LLMs)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="297" data-end="398">
<p data-start="299" data-end="398">Substack essays and working notes (non–peer-reviewed but citable as long as we mark them correctly)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="400" data-end="421">We will cite them as:</p>
<ol data-start="423" data-end="635">
<li data-start="423" data-end="482">
<p data-start="426" data-end="482"><strong data-start="426" data-end="460">Preprint / Working manuscripts</strong> (if titles are known)</p>
