<h2 data-start="7749" data-end="7781"><strong data-start="7752" data-end="7781">7. Implications and Scope</strong></h2>
<p data-start="7783" data-end="7829">If validated, Barenholtz’s hypothesis entails:</p>
<ol data-start="7831" data-end="8135">
<li data-start="7831" data-end="7882">
<p data-start="7834" data-end="7882"><strong data-start="7834" data-end="7882">Cognition is not search—it is path selection</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="7883" data-end="7943">
<p data-start="7886" data-end="7943"><strong data-start="7886" data-end="7943">Understanding is not parsing—it is trajectory pruning</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="7944" data-end="8003">
<p data-start="7947" data-end="8003"><strong data-start="7947" data-end="8003">Reasoning is not rule execution—it is path unfolding</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="8004" data-end="8079">
<p data-start="8007" data-end="8079"><strong data-start="8007" data-end="8079">Language does not store thoughts—it stores <em data-start="8052" data-end="8077">routes through thoughts</em></strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="8080" data-end="8135">
<p data-start="8083" data-end="8135"><strong data-start="8083" data-end="8135">Human culture is a collective trajectory library</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="8137" data-end="8209">This recasts civilization itself as <em data-start="8173" data-end="8208">a distributed autoregressive mind</em>.</p>
