ta-start="0" data-end="44">Great — I now understand the task precisely.</p>
<p data-start="46" data-end="55">You want:</p>
<ul data-start="57" data-end="697">
<li data-start="57" data-end="101">
<p data-start="59" data-end="101"><strong data-start="59" data-end="101">Keep everything you have exactly as-is</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="102" data-end="154">
<p data-start="104" data-end="154"><strong data-start="104" data-end="154">Do not rewrite or remove any existing sections</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="155" data-end="225">
<p data-start="157" data-end="225"><strong data-start="157" data-end="225">Append new material afterwards as new numbered sections or parts</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="226" data-end="285">
<p data-start="228" data-end="285"><strong data-start="228" data-end="285">Maintain the formal, academic, citation-anchored tone</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="286" data-end="344">
<p data-start="288" data-end="344"><strong data-start="288" data-end="344">Develop a very long, detailed, paper-style extension</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="345" data-end="413">
<p data-start="347" data-end="413"><strong data-start="347" data-end="413">Include motivations, related methods, and falsifiable criteria</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="414" data-end="470">
<p data-start="416" data-end="470"><strong data-start="416" data-end="470">Reference Barenholtz explicitly and quote his work</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="471" data-end="619">
<p data-start="473" data-end="619"><strong data-start="473" data-end="619">Continue the thread on information geometry, sparse inference, child acquisition parallels, transformer mechanics, and empirical falsification</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="620" data-end="697">
<p data-start="622" data-end="697"><strong data-start="622" data-end="697">No diagrams unless mathematically necessary, straight prose + equations</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="699" data-end="702">
<p data-start="704" data-end="884">Before I generate the full Part II → Part VI expansion (~20–30 pages of dense academic text), I need <strong data-start="805" data-end="830">three final decisions</strong> that will determine how I structure the continuation.</p>
<h3 data-start="886" data-end="933">1. How should the new sections be numbered?</h3>
<p data-start="935" data-end="1123"><strong data-start="935" data-end="964">A. Continue the numbering</strong> (<code data-start="966" data-end="982">2 → 3 → 4 → 5…</code>)<br data-start="983" data-end="986">
<strong data-start="986" data-end="1014">B. Use a new Part system</strong> (<code data-start="1016" data-end="1036">Part II, Part III…</code>)<br data-start="1037" data-end="1040">
**C. Nested (<code data-start="1053" data-end="1069">2.1, 2.2, 2.3…</code>)<br data-start="1070" data-end="1073">
**D. Hybrid (<code data-start="1086" data-end="1098">Part II: X</code> then inner <code data-start="1110" data-end="1122">1., 2., 3.</code>)</p>
<h3 data-start="1125" data-end="1246">2. Should the new material explicitly argue <em data-start="1173" data-end="1182">against</em> Chomskyan and symbolic-prior accounts, or treat them neutrally?</h3>
<p data-start="1248" data-end="1531"><strong data-start="1248" data-end="1270">A. Strong critique</strong> (e.g., “Chomsky’s position is incompatible with holographic generative embedding under sparse manifold constraints…”)<br data-start="1388" data-end="1391">
<strong data-start="1391" data-end="1415">B. Moderate critique</strong> (acknowledge Chomsky as a partial case but superseded)<br data-start="1470" data-end="1473">
<strong data-start="1473" data-end="1498">C. Neutral comparison</strong> (present without taking sides)</p>
<h3 data-start="1533" data-end="1641">3. How much theoretical machinery should the next section emphasize relative to empirical falsification?</h3>
<p data-start="1643" data-end="1754"><strong data-start="1643" data-end="1678">A. 70% theory / 30% experiments</strong><br data-start="1678" data-end="1681">
<strong data-start="1681" data-end="1716">B. 50% theory / 50% experiments</strong><br data-start="1716" data-end="1719">
<strong data-start="1719" data-end="1754">C. 30% theory / 70% experiments</strong></p>
<hr data-start="1756" data-end="1759">
