01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% FUTURE WORK — Roadmap, Open Problems, and Experimental Frontiers</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>*{Future Work}

The framework developed here connects predictive geometry, sparse inference, attention dynamics, and embodied generative loops into a single account of linguistic and cognitive emergence. This synthesis opens multiple empirical, theoretical, and engineering directions. We group future work into five tightly-coupled research agendas.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{1. Geometry of Predictive Manifolds}

This paper formalizes semantic space as a Riemannian manifold endowed with the Fisher--Rao metric. Immediate research extensions include:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Computing </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{curvature spectra} (Ricci, sectional, and scalar curvature) of next-token manifolds in pretrained LLMs, and correlating them with reasoning complexity, surprisal profiles, and compositional reuse.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Characterizing </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{phase transitions} in manifold geometry across scale (model size, data quantity, training time) to determine whether reasoning ability corresponds to curvature flattening, dimensional collapse, or geodesic sparsification.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Evaluating whether human incremental sentence processing follows </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{shortest-path geodesics} in model manifolds, via eyetracking or self-paced reading datasets.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Testing whether logical contradiction, metaphor, and semantic anomaly occupy </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{negative-curvature regions}, predicting longer geodesics and higher predictive entropy.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{2. Mechanistic Tests of Auto-Autoregression}

Barenholtz’s ``auto-autoregressive'' hypothesis predicts that learned predictors internalize their own continuation machinery. Future tests include:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Identifying whether transformers implement </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{internal hypothesis enumeration loops} during multi-step reasoning, detectable via recurrent attention motifs or cyclic state visitation.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Probing for </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{implicit world-simulators} by ablating components suspected to store reusable transition templates and measuring collapses in sample efficiency.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Testing whether successive transformer layers implement </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{iterative posterior sharpening} akin to belief propagation or Kalman-style smoothing.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Measuring representational </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{hysteresis} across long-horizon predictions to detect when a model becomes ``committed'' to a latent trajectory.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{3. Biological and Developmental Validation}

The cognitive interpretation of predictive geometry makes strong claims about human learning, none of which require language-specific priors. Experiments to evaluate this include:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Comparing child and model learning curves on </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{synthetic holographic-linguistic agnostic grammars} to test whether both rely on sparse template reuse rather than symbolic rule induction.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Measuring whether human learners show </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{sharp posterior collapse} onto a small set of continuations during comprehension, via information-theoretic analysis of eye movement entropy.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Testing whether infants exhibit </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{geodesic bias} in sequence learning tasks—preferring low-curvature transitions over high-curvature, even when transition probability is controlled.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Using MEG/EEG decoding to evaluate whether neural next-word prediction signatures exhibit </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{natural gradient-like error propagation}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{4. Scaling Laws and Efficiency Constraints}

If language learning is sparse predictive inference, then efficiency—not data size—determines asymptotic behavior. Future work will examine:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Whether scaling laws break when </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{posterior sparsity saturates}, predicting a regime where additional parameters add diminishing linguistic generalization.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Training small models with explicit </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{sparsity penalties on predictive hypothesis support}, testing whether this yields large-model generalization benchmarks with fewer parameters.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Measuring </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{sample efficiency as a function of manifold intrinsic dimensionality} rather than parameter count.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{5. Interpretability and Causal Interventions}

The geometric hypothesis yields unusually precise mechanistic probes:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Geodesic intervention}: steering hidden states along low-curvature directions and testing whether reasoning success rates improve.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Curvature surgery}: artificially flattening or sharpening local manifold curvature and evaluating effects on logical consistency, hallucination rate, and compositionality.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Posterior-editing interventions}: rewriting internal attention distributions to match the analytically-derived sparse posterior, and measuring alignment with Bayes-optimal predictions.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Counterfactual gradient routing}: forcing updates along or orthogonal to estimated Fisher directions to test whether learning performance is governed by natural-gradient alignment.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{Grand Challenge Questions}

These projects collectively aim to resolve a deeper scientific question:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{center}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textit</span></span><span>{Is language intelligence the discovery of latent generative geometry under constraints of sparse continuation, rather than the acquisition of syntactic rules or symbolic primitives?}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{center}

If correct, the consequences extend beyond linguistics and AI. Language would cease to be a special cognitive module or a cultural artifact encoded in the brain, and instead be understood as the </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{unavoidable equilibrium} of any sufficiently efficient system trained to recursively predict itself under limited bandwidth.

---

